-- CK-303: R-5.8.9 (#957) and, as CK-304, R-5.8.10 (#412): Conduit's entry,
-- unchanged (`_expected.sources`), on browser-tea with enforcement.
-- R-5.8.9: `update`'s arms are told apart, and Conduit's view events carry
-- only `Cred` and strings, so the four model records at `Main.beni:254`
-- (`model#Article.0.article#Loaded.0`, the two `feed#Loaded.0#Model.0`,
-- `model#Settings.0.status#Loaded.0`) are accepted `entry`. v1 refuses them
-- `payload` (approx): it joins the arms (§20.5, §23.6).
-- R-5.8.10: the `ChangedUrl` address is a new record at every event and
-- `update` does not keep it, so `msg#ChangedUrl.0` is accepted `entry`. v1
-- refuses it `escaped` (approx).
-- R-4.8.15 (#410, CK-292): the form `update` moves between the variants of
-- `model#Editor.1.status` is not a second holder, so its four lines are
-- accepted `entry`. v1 refuses them `disjoint`.
-- The golden is `ownership/Conduit`'s with those nine lines and the counts
-- changed.
